DESCRIPTION:Kwanzaa is a seven-day celebration of African American family\,
  community\, and culture that runs from December 26 through January 1. Mau
 lana Karenga created it in 1966\, and each day is given to one of the Nguz
 o Saba\, the seven principles at the center of the holiday.\n\nhttps://tod
 aycelebrates.com/holiday/kwanzaa/
